se camera  lenses are now of course the 13s don't  have the three times telephoto that  comes with the 13 pro  but other than that if you guys want to  see how the cameras compare to say the  iphone 12s  or the 12 pro max you guys could  actually go and check out my camera  comparison that's very detailed and if  you're wondering is it really worth the  pro camera to get that extra telephoto  and the other updates such as the larger  sensor i actually have a video that came  out i think that was yesterday posted  you guys can check that out and see if  that telephoto really makes a difference  for you along with the upgraded ultra  wide lens now those videos are available  but let's see how much better is the 13  mini's camera compared to the single  camera that is on the iphone se here's a  regular shot in normal lighting and you  guys can see how much more detail we  have with the new mini and here's a shot  with night mode which of course the sc  does not have it looks so much better  having that capability and then with the  front facing state camera we also have  night mode it makes low light shots look  much better and much more detailed and  then if you're somebody that wants to  zoom without a telephoto here is how the  zoom shot looks with apple's upscaling  and then of course we have the ultra  wide lens which is very helpful and a  lot of different scenarios gives you  really nice angles and then a regular  selfie shot this has actually blur from  the portrait mode that you can get and  the same thing goes with portraits using  that standard lens that capability makes  your photos look a lot more professional  you can blur out background so if you're  somebody that's considering these phones  i would definitely say if you care about  camera quality at all  you have to go with the 13 mini so what  is my final verdict on the iphone 13  mini is it worth upgrading to from an  older iphone in even the iphone 12 mini  and is it worth buying instead of a much  cheaper iphone se and should you spend  more money potentially and get the 13 or  the same amount of money get the 12.  those are a lot of answers uh to give  you guys but i'll straight up say yes it  is worth it if you wanted a smaller  phone last year but you didn't go for it  buy it now if you cared about the  battery life and it wasn't good enough  now it is it even beats out the 12 and  the other features such as the better  processor brighter display and if you  like having a smaller phone i would buy  it instead of the iphone 12. now with  that said  if you have older phones and you kind of  like that smaller size i would still say  go for there's so many more improvements  for the extra money i would definitely  not get the 12 mini 400 less since that  is still for sale you get so many  improvements especially the antennas and  that reception that matters a lot and  much better battery life as well and  then the cameras and then compared to  the 13 well if you're somebody that  watches a lot of videos you listen to  music with the built-in speakers or you  play games having that larger screen  with the better speakers is nice but  outside of that unless you know you need  killer battery life the 13 mini still  delivers it has very little downsides  and you save a hundred dollars and have  a much more smaller compact phone that  just fits so nicely in the hand and then  that mini size with the wallet or the  mac safe power pack that works out  really well so this year i actually am  very happy with the 13 mini and  the last secret actually  is that right now based on all the info  we have apple is not going to be making  another mini phone so if you wanted to  upgrade from an older iphone or from the  12 mini or you just want a small phone  it is worth buying it this year with the  13 mini with that new processor the  better cameras because going into the  future it looks like apple is going to  have a new version of the se a cheaper  one that is not going to 